================================================================================
STAGE 2 — dynamic params (add/remove at runtime), PARAMS RESYNC
================================================================================
Not built yet. Forcing case: contexts/clap_plugins.c's clap_plug_ext_
params_rescan already handles CLAP_PARAM_RESCAN_VALUES/TEXT/INFO for real
(position-only updates to existing params). Its CLAP_PARAM_RESCAN_ALL
branch (param count/order/ids changed) is still a TODO stub - the naive
fix (destroy the whole container and rebuild) is wrong: it would give
every surviving param a brand-new ContextId even when it didn't actually
change, breaking the CROSS-CUTTING INVARIANT above and any UI/CX reference
pointed at a param that's still logically the same one.

Algorithm (DECIDED) - params_container_resync(container, new_params[],
new_count), called by the owner (CLAP's RESCAN_ALL handler today) with its
current full param list, matched by uid not position:
  pass 1 (removals) - for each currently-alive slot whose uid is no longer
    in new_params: release owned state, mark the slot dead/tombstoned, do
    NOT shift anything.
  pass 2 (additions) - for each new_params[i] with no matching alive slot:
    reuse a tombstoned slot if one exists, else grow rt_params/ui_params
    by one (realloc). Populate PRM_PARAM_RT (val, min_val, max_val, val_
    changed=0, uid, cookie) and PRM_PARAM_UI (val, min_val, max_val,
    def_val=val, inc_am, name, uid, is_hidden=0) exactly like param_add_
    param does today - plus an alive flag on both, new field.
  survivors (uid in both) - untouched by either pass. Value/name refresh
    for survivors is RESCAN_VALUES/INFO's job already, not this function's.
  Both arrays get identical treatment, same slot index. Safe to mutate
  both directly, no ring-buffer messaging needed for the structural part -
  CLAP only allows RESCAN_ALL while the plugin is deactivated (existing
  `if (plug->plug_inst_activated == 1) return;` guard), so the rt thread
  isn't reading rt_params for that plugin while this runs.
  This function does NOT report what changed to anyone - it only leaves
  the container in the correct new state. STAGE 3's CX resync discovers
  what changed later by re-walking child_at and diffing, same as it
  already does for every other container.
Needs: an alive/tombstone bool on both PRM_PARAM_RT and PRM_PARAM_UI;
param_find_uid already exists and is reused as-is. Array growth: realloc
to exact size on demand (rescans are rare/cold, not a hot path) - no
doubling-growth needed.

Once this lands: revisit whether stage 3's CX-child wiring needs any of
the same growth logic duplicated, or can call this directly.

================================================================================
STAGE 3 — parameters as CX contexts, integrated into the action system
================================================================================
Agreed direction: params become CX tree nodes (like plugin instances),
not a live external list (like JACK ports - those stay non-CX because
they're externally driven/churny; params are owned entirely by this app).

Open questions (not decided):
- Materialize every parameter as a CX child, or only non-hidden ones
  (PRM_PARAM_UI.is_hidden already exists)? Check real per-plugin param
  counts (tens to low hundreds possible) against how the rest of the CX
  tree scales before committing.

Decided pieces:
- Value changes go through the (ui-side) param_set_value and its existing
  ring-buffer message to rt - matches the JACK/plugins pattern already,
  no new plumbing expected. param_set_value_rt is rt-originated only, not
  relevant to action_do.
- How params become CX children / how RESCAN_ALL reaches app_intrf: reuses
  the existing generic resync pipeline as-is (app_intrf's child diff/
  DATA_EVENT_CHILDREN_CHANGED already handles any child kind, zero new
  code needed there). What's actually new: sample_ops/lv2_plugin_ops/
  clap_plugin_ops/synth-osc ops currently stub child_at to `return false`
  - these need real child_at/child_count backed by PRM_CONTAIN (needs
  STAGE 2 first). Each owning instance needs its own instance-scoped
  params_dirty bool (distinct from the container-level plugins_dirty/
  samples_dirty, which mean "the SET of instances changed"), set right
  after params_container_resync finishes and checked inside the existing
  per-cycle rt-to-ui message loop (clap_read_rt_to_ui_messages today;
  LV2/synth/sampler would need the equivalent once/if they get dynamic
  params too).
- DataActionType(s) for changing a value: DATA_ACTION_SET_VALUE (one
  numeric arg, the value) and DATA_ACTION_ADJUST_VALUE (one signed step
  COUNT, not a raw value - action_do maps sign to Operation_Increase/
  Decrease). Not three separate actions (inc/dec are the same op with a
  sign). Not SET_VALUE-only with the UI computing current+increment
  itself - what a step means is owner-defined behaviour, UI triggers,
  owner decides. Both map to existing param_set_value(container, val_id,
  set_to, NULL, Operation_...) one-liners in action_do, no new params.c
  logic. Other paramOperType values (DefValue/SetIncr/SetDefValue/
  ChangeName/ToggleHidden) stay unexposed to the action system until
  something actually needs them.
- DATA_ACTION_SET_CHOICE for CLAP_PARAM_IS_ENUM params: an enum param is
  a CHOICE in disguise (CLAP spec: IS_ENUM implies IS_STEPPED, contiguous
  min..max, every value has a real value_to_text() label) - reuse list_at/
  DataChoice exactly like the plugin catalogue does, list_at walks
  min..max calling param_get_value_as_string per step for the label
  (that function's value-is-caller-supplied signature exists specifically
  for this). Reuses helper_choice_list_step as-is on the CLI side.
  Considered and rejected: making an enum param an ordinary SET_VALUE/
  ADJUST_VALUE param and having the UI itself loop min..max to build a
  picker - that pushes "this param's domain is a walkable range" (owner-
  specific domain knowledge) into the UI, the same anti-pattern already
  rejected for ADJUST_VALUE's step semantics. Not implemented yet.
- Param categories: PRM_PARAM_UI gets a category/module string field
  (CLAP: clap_param_info_t.module, "Oscillators/Wavetable 1" style paths).
  Params stay FLAT CX children of their owning instance; category is
  presentational metadata only, not a real tree level (an intermediate
  CX node per category was considered and rejected - no side channel to
  scope child_at by category the way list_at has `partial`, and CLAP's
  "module can change via RESCAN_INFO without add/remove" doesn't fit CX's
  fixed-at-creation parentage). child_at should return params sorted by
  category so a UI can print a header over contiguous runs without a real
  tree node. Not implemented yet - add the field + an accessor when
  actually wiring params into a UI.

