  Revisit only when specifically decided to build either.

================================================================================
FUTURE - categories for CHOICE / MULTI_CHOICE lists (design sketch, not
scheduled - needed once plugin preset browsers are built: LV2 preset
banks/CLAP preset factories are essentially always categorised)
================================================================================
No new DataListId/DataArgKind/DataActionType needed - still a flat,
idx-enumerable list_at. Two additions to data_actions.h:
- DataChoice gains DATA_CHOICE_CATEGORY (1u << 1), alongside the existing
  DATA_CHOICE_LINKED (1u << 0) - a row with this bit set is a node to
  descend into, not a pickable leaf (like a directory vs a file in one
  flat readdir).
- DataActionReq gains a top-level field, sibling to `type`, outside the
  per-action union: `uint64_t category_scope;` (0 = list root). Set by the
  UI while drilling; ignored by list_at for non-categorised lists. Must be
  a dedicated top-level field, not a reused union field (e.g. NOT add_
  choice.choice_value) - CONNECT's targets list already needs its own
  union field (source) live at the same time as a drill scope would be,
  so reusing a union field collides for that action shape.

CLI-side drilling: one more branch in the existing "on SELECTED" handling
already used by helper_choice_list_step's callers - category row updates
category_scope/resets cursor and re-browses the same list; leaf row
behaves exactly as it does today (return, for a pick-and-return list like
CONNECT's SOURCE; act-and-loop, for a repeating list like ADD_CHOICE).
Backing out (h/ESC) needs a small caller-owned breadcrumb stack (scope,
cursor) per level drilled into, capped like ACTION_ARG_COUNT elsewhere in
this CLI - no heap.

Two things any list_at needs to get right once built:
- A category node's DataChoice.value must hash its FULL path (e.g.
  fnv1a64("Bass/Analog/Warm")), not just its own name, or two different
  parents with a same-named child collide.
- Only the immediate parent's scope value is ever needed by list_at, not
  the whole ancestor chain (same as CONNECT's one-level source/target
  dependency) - the CLI's breadcrumb stack is for visual backing-out only.

Rejected: a dedicated tree-enumeration call (not a new interaction shape,
just "pick from a list" applied recursively - violates "a new arg kind is
the only thing that should touch the UI"); returning a nested tree from
one list_at call (breaks the flat-pagination contract every caller
relies on, needs heap-allocated variable-depth structures crossing data_
actions.h's dependency-free boundary).
